      "**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"Raindrop Workshop Gives AI Agents a Local Debugger\", \"link\": \"https://awesomeagents.ai/news/raindrop-workshop-open-source-agent-debugger/\", \"content\": \"Raindrop Workshop Gives AI Agents a Local Debugger. Raindrop's MIT-licensed Workshop streams every token and tool call from yo...\n                                                # Search Results: Raindrop Workshop AI Agent Debugger\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about **Raindrop Workshop**:\n\n## Overview\nRaindrop Workshop is an **open-source, local AI agent debugger** that was released in **May 2026**. It appears to be the first dedicated local debugging tool specifically designed for AI agents.\n\n## Key Features\n- **Local debugging**: Enables you to debug AI agents locally rather than relying on cloud-based dashboards\n- **Token-by-token tracing**: Streams every token and tool call from your AI agent\n- **Open source**: MIT-licensed and freely available\n- **MCP-native**: Built with Model Context Protocol integration\n- **One-command installation**: Easy to set up\n\n## Key Dates & Milestones\n- **May 14, 2026**: Official launch day\n  - Hit 200 GitHub stars on the first day\n  - Received first pull request\n  - Featured on Product Hunt homepage\n  - Significant social media engagement (2.5K views on launch posts)\n\n## Use Cases\n- Debugging AI agents that fail at inconvenient times (e.g., 1 AM) without needing to access SaaS dashboards\n- Integrating with Claude Code to read traces, write evals, and fix bugs\n- Local trace streaming for instant debugging\n\n## Availability\n- Available on GitHub (open source)\n- Featured on Product Hunt\n- Active on social media platforms (Twitter/X, LinkedIn, Instagram)\n- Official website: raindrop.ai\n\nThe tool addresses a common pain point for AI agent developers who need to debug locally without relying on external dashboards or cloud services."
